# Line endings are a property of the REPO, not of the machine that happens to clone it.
#
# The predecessor project has no .gitattributes and relies on `core.autocrlf=true` in the
# system gitconfig. That has cost it nothing in 822 commits — but it is a machine setting,
# and it survives neither a fresh machine nor a contributor with `autocrlf=false`.
#
# Named cost: `eol=lf` forces LF in the WORKING TREE, which `autocrlf=true` does not. Windows
# tooling that expects CRLF will see LF here. That is the trade, made knowingly.
* text=auto eol=lf
